# The SNOT Troubleshooting Strategy

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box; word-wrap: break-word; overflow-wrap: break-word;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Troubleshooting</strong> is a form of problem-solving that involves using a logical and systematic search for the source of a problem.</p>
</div>

#### The SNOT Strategy provides a structured approach for troubleshooting problems, helping students develop independence and critical thinking skills when faced with challenges.

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
  <p style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <b>Step 1: Self</b> <br><br> Restate the problem and make your best guesses about possible solutions. 
</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
  <p style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <b>Step 2: Neighbor</b> <br><br>
    Talk through the problem with someone to share viewpoints and narrow down possibilities.
</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
  <p style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <b>Step 3: Online Resources</b> <br><br>
    Search message boards, technical manuals, FAQs and other online resources to further narrow down possible solutions.
</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #F5F7F8; color: #000000; padding: 15px; border-radius: 10px; width: 90%; margin: 20px auto;">
  <p style = "font-size:14pt;">
    <b>Step 4: Technical Expert</b> <br><br>
    Ask a technical or subject-matter expert that can provide guidance.

</p>
</div>

<div style="background-color: #a6e3e8; border-radius: 40px; color: #000000; width: 95%; padding: 1px 20px 1px 20px;">

<p style="line-height: 1.5; margin-left: 10px; margin-right: 10px; margin-top: 10px; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 18px; "><strong>Teacher Tip:</strong> Having a clear troubleshooting strategy like SNOT encourages students to become problem-solvers instead of immediately seeking help. It builds resilience, promotes collaboration, and teaches them how to find and evaluate reliable resources—an essential skill for coding, data science, and beyond.    
</p>
</div>


## Let's try a troubleshooting activity


